---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
import Command from './Command.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import download from '../data/downloads.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<section id="setup" class="setup section" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
  <div class="container setup-grid">
    <div>
      <SectionHeading index="06" label="Start here" title="Make it your workflow." id="setup-title">
        <p>Python 3.10+, a project on your PC, and a running inference worker. Start with the current V1 source preview.</p>
      </SectionHeading>
      <div class="setup-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href={`${base}downloads/freecompute-v1-source.zip`} download>Download source preview <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${base}guide/`}>Open the setup guide <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
      <p class="setup-version">v{download.version} beta · Source install · Apache 2.0</p>
    </div>
    <div class="setup-instructions">
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Install the CLI.</strong><span>Extract the source preview and install it in a Python virtual environment. The guide has Windows, Linux and macOS commands.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Start your worker.</strong><span>Upload the current Kaggle notebook. Keep the same private API key in Kaggle Secrets and your local <code>.env</code>.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Connect from your terminal.</strong><span>Run from the source checkout with the fresh URL printed by Kaggle. Use <code>--workspace</code> to select your project.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <Command label="Connect your text worker" command={'freecompute --remote-url "PASTE-KAGGLE-URL-HERE"'} />
      <p class="reconnect-note">Tunnel changed? Use <code>/connect PASTE-KAGGLE-URL-HERE</code> in the CLI. It reuses your key for this run; active or uncertain requests must be resolved first.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
